    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d468-a1">

                <pb facs="0555" n="475" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg475"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Lansdowne, to Mr. Choate</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-06-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 28,
                    1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I referred to His Majesty’s
                    secretary of state for war the copies of dispatches addressed to your excellency
                    by the United States Government, asking for the release of two United States
                    citizens, Messrs. F. Connelly and W. Smith, who are detained as prisoners of war
                    in Ceylon and St. Helena, respectively.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to inform your excellency that I learn from Mr. Secretary
                    Brodrick that he is unable to make exceptions in the cases of individual
                    prisoners of war unless they are suffering from serious or dangerous illness,
                    and consequently regrets that he does not see his way to ordering the release of
                    Messrs. Connelly and W. Smith.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansdowne</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
